    "answer": "You can write out the exact fixed sequence of steps a task always follows. Which architecture is right, and why?\n\n- ✅ **A.** A workflow, because the path is known and coding it avoids the cost and nondeterminism of an agent\n- **B.** An agent, because agents are more capable and future-proof and you can always constrain it later if the extra latency and cost become a problem in production\n- **C.** A single mega-prompt containing all steps\n- **D.** Independent, unordered calls\n\n**Правильно:** A\n\nA known, fixed path is a workflow: deterministic and cheaper. Reaching for an agent adds nondeterminism and cost you do not need, and a mega-prompt or unordered calls cannot reliably sequence the work."
